{title: Steadfast Love}
{subtitle: Genesis 39:1–23}
{key: G}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | [G] | [Em] | [C] |
| [D] | [G] | [Em] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Joseph [G]was taken down to Egypt land
Potip[Em]har bought him from the Ishmaelites
The Lord [C]was with him and he prospered
His [D]master saw the favor of the Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He put [G]Joseph in charge of the house
And en[Em]trusted all his wealth to care
The [C]Lord blessed the field and the home
[D]And Joseph was handsome and well built
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
After [C]some time his master’s wife
Took [G]notice of him and spoke
[Am]Come to bed with me she said
But he refused [D]her with a voice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
How could I [G]do such a great [Em]evil
And [C]sin against God in this [D]place
The Lord was [G]with him in the pri[Em]son
And [C]showed him [D]steadfast [G]love
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Day after day she kept at him
But [Em]he would not listen or lie
[C]One day he came to do his work
She [D]caught his cloak and screamed aloud
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
She told the [C]men of the household
That he [G]came to make sport of us
She [Am7]kept his cloak until his master
Came [D]home and heard her story
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
His master burned with anger then
And [Em]took him to the prison cell
Where [C]the king’s prisoners were held
[D]And there he remained alone
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[G]The warden paid no attention
[Em]To anything under his [C]care
Because the Lord was with him
[D]And gave him success in [G]all
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
